The Self-service Library Stations launched by the Hong Kong Public Libraries provide the following round-the-clock services:

- Borrowing library materials (more than 300 items are stored for library card holders to borrow);
- Returning library materials from any public library, with borrowing records updated immediately;
- Picking up reserved library materials;
- Paying library fees and charges, such as reservation fees and overdue fines, using Octopus cards, with payment records updated immediately.

These services are available at stations located in Hong Kong Island, Kowloon, and the New Territories.
